# Pinned zero-model canary outcomes for eval/harness_acceptance.sh (engine pin: FORGE_COMMIT).
# Re-pin DELIBERATELY, with the commit that moved a number, never to make a run pass.
# floor/floor never builds a play menu; random/random reaches the full menu (see CLAUDE.md).
floor.seed=42
floor.winner=A
floor.turns=108
# 2026-10-12: G7 routed chooseStartingPlayer/chooseColor/chooseSomeType/chooseProtectionType then
# chooseCardsToDiscardToMaximumHandSize/chooseCardsToDelve from Forge AI to the model. The floor arm
# now takes the deterministic fronts (was AI); decisions moved 1004 -> 1005 -> 1053 (same winner/turns).
# 2026-10-13: engine pin bumped c1c64a53 -> 6c1810dd0b42 (3 months upstream). The floor arm is
# deterministic, but the ENGINE changed (card scripts, AI, rules handling). Same winner AND turns;
# decisions 1053 -> 1064. Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0, game not capped.
# 2026-10-13 (later): the seat may respond to its OWN trigger on the stack (it used to auto-pass
# without a row). The floor arm reaches that window 4 times and takes its usual
# play(no-budget)->PASS, so 4 more auto rows are written: 1064 -> 1068. Same winner, same turns,
# no game action changed. Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0.
floor.decisions=1068
random.seed=42
# 2026-09-07: model-owned optional confirmations expose four previously silent AI
# trigger choices to the random policy (first divergence: confirm-trigger, turn 15, decision 61).
# 2026-10-12: G7 routing (above) now exposes play/draw, colour, type, protection, cleanup-discard and
# delve choices to the random policy too; the game diverges far earlier. Reproduced.
# 2026-10-12 (later): simultaneous-trigger ORDER is model-owned too; the random policy now permutes
# trigger order, moving the game again (17 turns / 75 decisions, winner B). Reproduced.
# 2026-10-13: engine pin bumped c1c64a53 -> 6c1810dd0b42. The random arm is a random walk over the
# legal menu, so ANY engine change re-rolls the whole game: now winner A, 29 turns / 167 decisions.
# Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0, game not capped. Random is a floor ANCHOR, not a
# behavioural contract -- its job is to move deterministically under a fixed engine, which it does.
# 2026-10-13 (later): sacrifice-as-cost moved from Forge AI to the seat on the real play path
# (playChosenSpellAbility override; see OWNERSHIP.md "Correction"). The random arm now makes those
# choices itself -- 13 sacrifice decisions appear in the game log that were previously silent -- so
# the random walk re-rolls: winner A, 26 turns / 171 decisions. Floor is unchanged (it never plays).
# Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0, game not capped.
# 2026-10-13 (later): one creature that can attack, and one scried or surveiled card, are decisions
# again instead of "forced-only-legal" shortcuts (attack with it / keep it, unasked). The random arm
# now rolls those too, so its walk re-rolls: winner B, 19 turns / 65 decisions. Reproduced twice
# (/tmp/acc-fbef9cfab, /tmp/acc-part). Floor is unchanged: it attacks with everything and never scries.
random.winner=B
random.turns=19
